codex
I found a structural saving: the first preactivation is exactly Gaussian with covariance `W.T @ W`, so the probe cloud can be sampled directly in that preactivation space and whitened to the exact covariance. That avoids the first `x @ W` probe multiply while preserving the intended first-layer distribution.
apply patch
